<div id="export-panel" style="display: none;">
  <div class="oscar-export">
    <p class="oscar-export-lead">
      This saves your interface as one HTML file. Open it on a tablet, a phone
      or another computer &mdash; there is nothing else to install and nothing
      to unzip.
    </p>

    <!-- The misunderstanding behind every "my exported page does nothing"
         report. It is stated before the button, not after it. -->
    <div class="oscar-export-warning">
      <strong>OSCAR has to stay running.</strong>
      A browser cannot send OSC on its own, so the exported page hands every
      message to OSCAR, which puts it on the network. Keep OSCAR running on the
      address below, and make sure the device showing the page can reach it.
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
      <label for="export-name">File name</label>
      <input
        id="export-name"
        class="form-control"
        type="text"
        placeholder="my-interface"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="form-row">
      <div class="form-group col-8">
        <label for="export-host">OSCAR is reachable at</label>
        <input id="export-host" class="form-control" type="text" />
      </div>
      <div class="form-group col-4">
        <label for="export-port">Bridge port</label>
        <input id="export-port" class="form-control" type="number" min="1" max="65535" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="oscar-export-hint">
      Use the address other devices see, not <code>localhost</code>, unless the
      page will only ever be opened on this computer. You can change it later
      without exporting again: add
      <code>?oscar-host=&hellip;&amp;oscar-port=&hellip;</code> to the page's
      address.
    </p>

    <div id="export-error" class="oscar-export-error" style="display: none;"></div>

    <button id="export-button" class="btn btn-gradient btn-block" type="button">
      Download the interface
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
